# MHA, GQA or MQA, at which learning rate? Six runs of a 12-layer Llama, in one file.
#
#   bux plan  examples/experiments/attention_ablation.bux
#   bux train examples/experiments/attention_ablation.bux --only mqa
#
# The architecture and the recipe come from other files, by name. Definitions here
# take the place of theirs everywhere, so llama3_8b's `block` picks up this `attn`.
use llama3_8b
use fineweb_wsd

# Llama 3 8B, scaled down.
d_model = 768
ffn.intermediate_size = 2048
model = embed block^12 norm head(tied=true)

# Three attentions, crossed with two learning rates: 3 × 2 runs.
attn.num_heads    = 12
attn.num_kv_heads = mha: 12 | gqa: 4 | mqa: 1
optimizer.lr      = 1e-3 | 3e-3

budget = 3B
